Hi Mara,

Thanks for making time this morning, especially on workshop day. Putting the
main points in writing so Lionel and Ezinne have them too - I know your
notetaker sends its own summary, but I'd rather we had it from me.

1) Weights. As agreed on the call, let's weight data terms at 30% in the
   writing-tool scorecard, given Agnieszka's note on the DPA. Whatever we
   buy has to live with those terms for years, and I'd rather the scorecard
   said so plainly than have it come up at contract stage. Lionel, copying
   you since it moves the scoring.

2) News: I've been confirmed as Registrar as of this week - no more
   "interim"! I'm still getting used to signing it without the extra word.

3) DSA. Ezinne (Dr. Marlowe-Abara, our VP for Academic Affairs, cc'd) will
   countersign the DSA for Saltmarren - it's with her office now. I'll get
   the countersigned copy back to you by next Tuesday. Ezinne, thank you
   for turning this around quickly; Mara is the system-office lead on the
   discovery.

4) Advising. I've thought more about what Tillie raised on Tuesday.
   Let's split it out and treat advising scheduling as its own project,
   separate from the transfer work - transfer students waiting weeks for
   an advising appointment is a real problem, but it's a different
   problem from transcript evaluation, and I don't want it to swallow
   the discovery. The wait-time data you promised Tillie belongs with
   the advising scheduling work now. Tillie leads our side. Can you
   scope a two-week discovery sprint with her? Nothing elaborate - what
   you'd look at, who you'd need, and what we'd know at the end of the
   two weeks.

   That puts the transfer discovery back where we started: transcript
   evaluation. For now it's waiting on the DSA. Next step on that side is
   Ezinne's countersignature, then the anonymized baseline sample can come
   to you. Until then I know the baseline data, and your baseline analysis,
   are stuck - no change there. I'd still like to hold the readout for
   19 March if we can.

5) Essay volumes: Rufus is pulling last year's ENGL 101/102 essay volumes
   - you'll have them Monday. (I know I said today on the call; he has the
   cleaner numbers.)

Good luck this afternoon - I hear the workshop is full.

Warmly,
Delphine

